[h1]Your SteelSeries RGB gear lights up only when the colony needs you.[/h1]

Alt-tabbed while the game runs at 3× speed? RimSense turns your SteelSeries mouse, keyboard or headset into a quiet colony alarm. It stays out of the way until something actually needs you — then tells you how urgent it is at a glance.

[h2]One simple rule[/h2]
[b]Color = how serious. Flashing = it just started. Steady = still going.[/b]

[table]
[tr][th]Light[/th][th]When[/th][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Red[/b] — 10 fast flashes, then steady[/td][td]Hostiles on a map with your colonists: raids, manhunters, infestations, berserk colonists[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Amber[/b] — 3 slow flashes, then steady[/td][td]A colonist in trouble (serious mental break, bleeding out, giving birth) or a large fire[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Your own lighting[/td][td]Everything else — RimSense hands control back to SteelSeries GG[/td][/tr]
[/table]

No mood bars, no weather colors, no day/night effects. If the light changes, it means something.

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Every SteelSeries RGB device[/b] — mice, keyboards, headsets, mousepads
[*][b]Customizable in GG[/b] — change colors or zones in GG → Engine → Apps → RimWorld → Configure
[*][b]In-game settings[/b] — toggle danger, attention and flashing in Options → Mod settings → RimSense
[*][b]Safe[/b] — no Harmony patches, no DLC required, safe to add to an existing save
[*][b]Lightweight[/b] — one check per second; networking never blocks the game
[*][b]Languages[/b] — English, Ukrainian, Russian
[/list]

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*]RimWorld 1.6 (Royalty, Ideology and Biotech are optional)
[*][url=https://steelseries.com/gg]SteelSeries GG[/url] running on Windows or macOS
[/list]
The first time you play with RimSense, a [b]RimWorld[/b] card appears in GG → Engine → Apps. That's where you can switch it off or change colors.

[h2]FAQ[/h2]
[b]The lights don't change.[/b] Open Options → Mod settings → RimSense and check the status line. It should say "SteelSeries GG: connected". Also make sure the RimWorld card in GG → Engine → Apps is ON.

[b]Does it work without DLC?[/b] Yes. Events from DLC you don't own are simply never triggered.

[b]Linux?[/b] SteelSeries GG doesn't exist on Linux, so RimSense quietly does nothing there.

[h2]Open source[/h2]
RimSense is free and open source (MIT). Code, bug reports and ideas: [url=https://github.com/Shramkoweb/RimSense]github.com/Shramkoweb/RimSense[/url]
If you like it, a thumbs up here or a star on GitHub helps a lot!

[hr][/hr]
[b]Українською:[/b] пристрої SteelSeries світяться лише тоді, коли колонії потрібні ви. Червоний — вороги, помаранчевий — колоніст у біді або пожежа. Мигає — щойно почалось, рівно — ще триває. Мод перекладено українською.

[b]По-русски:[/b] устройства SteelSeries светятся, только когда колонии нужны вы. Красный — враги, оранжевый — колонист в беде или пожар. Мигает — только началось, ровно — ещё длится.

